alex: Quick heads-up: onboarding sample using the JS SDK + edge runtime fails typechecks for people using ESM + strict tsconfig. Repro attached.

rina: saw this earlier — it's the generics + overload interactions when an ambient API returns unknown (Cloudflare env / D1 / KV). TS refuses to pick the object overload.

jorge: paste the minimal repro pls.

alex: repro:
```ts
// packages/sdk/src/index.ts (ESM d.ts emitted)
export function client(token: string): Client;
export function client(opts: { token?: string; refresh?: () => Promise<string> }): Client;
export function client(arg: any) { return new Client(arg); }

// examples/worker/src/index.ts
import { client } from '@redwood/sdk';
const c = client({ token: ENV.API_TOKEN }); // ENV.API_TOKEN typed as unknown by edge typings
c.doThing();
```

types-bot: TS ERROR: Argument of type '{ token: unknown; }' is not assignable to parameter of type 'string | { token?: string; refresh?: () => Promise<string> }'.

rina: the interesting bit: if you change the SDK to a single union signature `client(arg: string | { token?: string; refresh?: () => Promise<string> })` it compiles, but you lose the ergonomics of overloads (autocomplete shows both overloads in editors currently).

jorge: another angle: we can add an explicit fallback overload `export function client(arg: Record<string, unknown>): Client;` placed after the strict overloads — that lets unknown bind to something and keeps the richer overloads for normal uses.

alex: fallback overload seems safe. But worried about types drifting: we publish ESM .d.ts which tsc transforms differently for bundler/node16 resolutions. We need a CI matrix that compiles the example under multiple moduleResolution settings.

ci-bot: proposed job: ts-typing-edge-matrix: configs: [ {module: 'esnext', resolution: 'bundler'}, {module: 'es2020', resolution: 'node16'}, {module: 'commonjs', resolution: 'node'} ] — will run on PR.

rina: other small DX improvements: update the edge onboarding docs to include a short note about ambient unknowns and a tiny helper `const ensureString = (v: unknown) => typeof v === 'string' ? v : String(v);` instead of `as any` casts.

jorge: also add a unit test in examples that runs `tsc --noEmit` against the example with those tsconfigs so we catch regressions. Make the test part of the monorepo CI.

alex: one more weird flaky: when downstream project uses `moduleResolution: 'bundler'` + `skipLibCheck: false`, we still see the error even with fallback overload unless the d.ts order is exact. So PR should include a small note in CHANGELOG and explain the rationale (preserve strict overloads, add fallback to handle edge unknowns).

rina: agreed. Also ensure sample code avoids `as any` in the README — it teaches bad habits. Provide a short snippet that shows preferred pattern:
```ts
// recommended pattern for edge env values
const raw = ENV.MY_TOKEN; // unknown
const token = typeof raw === 'string' ? raw : String(raw);
const c = client({ token });
```

jorge: will draft PR: (1) add Record<string, unknown> fallback overload in types, (2) update examples, (3) add CI tsc matrix test, (4) changelog blurb.

alex: thanks. Filing DX-1427 and marking example blocked until PR merges. Will ping reviewers when ready.

